1
00:07:19,090 --> 00:07:25,090
Something evil has returned to Hogwarts!

2
00:14:38,181 --> 00:14:44,181
Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets is a adventure,
fantasy film directed by Chris Columbus.

3
00:21:57,272 --> 00:22:03,272
Cars fly, trees fight back, and a mysterious house-elf comes to warn
Harry Potter at the start of his second year at Hogwarts.

4
00:29:16,363 --> 00:29:22,363
Adventure and danger await when bloody writing on a wall
announces: The Chamber Of Secrets Has Been Opened.

5
00:36:35,454 --> 00:36:41,454
To save Hogwarts will require all of Harry, Ron and
Hermione's magical abilities and courage.

6
00:43:54,545 --> 00:44:00,545
Harry Potter, played by Daniel Radcliffe.

7
00:51:13,636 --> 00:51:19,636
Ron Weasley, played by Rupert Grint.

8
00:58:32,727 --> 00:58:38,727
Hermione Granger, played by Emma Watson.

9
01:05:51,818 --> 01:05:57,818
Gilderoy Lockhart, played by Kenneth Branagh.

10
01:13:10,909 --> 01:13:16,909
Dobby (voice), played by Toby Jones.

11
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:36,000
Rubeus Hagrid, played by Robbie Coltrane.

12
01:27:49,090 --> 01:27:55,090
Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets is a 2002 fantasy film directed
by Chris Columbus from a screenplay by Steve Kloves.

13
01:35:08,181 --> 01:35:14,181
It is based on the 1998 novel Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets by J.

14
01:42:27,272 --> 01:42:33,272
Produced by David Heyman, it is the sequel to Harry Potter and the Philosopher's
Stone (2001) and the second instalment in the Harry Potter film series.

15
01:49:46,363 --> 01:49:52,363
The film stars Daniel Radcliffe as Harry Potter, with Rupert Grint and Emma Watson
as his best friends Ron Weasley and Hermione Granger respectively.

16
01:57:05,454 --> 01:57:11,454
The story follows Harry's second year at Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry, where the Heir of Salazar
Slytherin opens the Chamber of Secrets, unleashing a monster that petrifies the school's students.

17
02:04:24,545 --> 02:04:30,545
The film was released in the United Kingdom and the United
States on 15 November 2002, by Warner Bros.

18
02:11:43,636 --> 02:11:49,636
It became a critical and commercial success, grossing $878 million worldwide (domestic 29.7%
and foreign 70.2%) and becoming the second-highest-grossing film of 2002.

19
02:19:02,727 --> 02:19:08,727
The film was nominated for many awards, including the BAFTA Award for Best
Production Design, Best Sound, and Best Special Visual Effects.

20
02:26:21,818 --> 02:26:27,818
It was followed by Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban (2004).

21
02:33:40,909 --> 02:33:46,909
The film explores themes of witch, flying car, elves, magic, sword.
